  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>(A) Aldehydes give red precipitate with Fehling&#39;s solution.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/867f40ec-83c6-4cbc-84e3-ef0f8165b49d.png\" style=\"width: 818px; height: 132px;\" /></p><p>(B) Phenols give violet colour with neutral ferric chloride solution</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7230d7ee-131d-4d6c-ab80-ebbf3bcbd335.png\" style=\"width: 623px; height: 187px;\" /></p><p>(C) Primary amines give isocyanides with chloroform in the presence of alkali. This reaction known as carbylamine reaction.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/1761f839-a0be-4578-822a-ce0242066e1e.png\" style=\"width: 396px; height: 162px;\" /></p><p>(D)&nbsp;1-phenylethanol give haloform reaction with sodium hypochlorite. The products are benzoate and chloroform.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/98585194-5acc-40c2-bf38-686c77fbed6c.png\" style=\"width: 550px; height: 140px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>",
